.TH CTPOOL_TRY_SUBMIT 3 "2026-08-02" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ctpool_try_submit \- submit a task without blocking
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadpool.h>

ccol_retval_t ctpool_try_submit(ctpool pool,
                                void (*fn)(void *),
                                void *arg,
                                void (*on_complete)(void *arg, bool ran));
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function is the same as ctpool_submit, with one difference. For a
bounded queue it never blocks. It returns ccol_container_full at once
when the queue is at capacity. For an unbounded queue it behaves
exactly as ctpool_submit does.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
pool         Thread pool handle
fn           Task function (must not be NULL)
arg          The library gives it to fn and on_complete (may be NULL)
on_complete  Called once for the task: on_complete(arg, true) after
             fn returns, or on_complete(arg, false) when the pool
             discards the task unrun (may be NULL)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success           - task enqueued.
ccol_invalid_args      - pool is CTPOOL_INVALID or a stale/already-destroyed handle, or fn is NULL.
ccol_not_enough_memory - task struct allocation failed.
ccol_not_permitted     - pool is shutting down.
ccol_container_full    - bounded queue is at capacity (not returned for
                         unbounded queues).
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ctpool_submit (3),
.BR ctpool_timed_submit (3)
